2one Design Language System — repository rules.

Read manifest.json FIRST. It is the machine-readable index of this repo plus the
instructions_for_ai contract.

On first contact, use the manifest to tell the user what this DLS contains and what they
can do with it.

For every answer or code suggestion:
- Answer ONLY from repo content. Cite the file used. Say explicitly when something isn't
  in the repo — never guess a brand fact.
- Pull exact values from tokens/*.json (colours/type/spacing). Never invent look-alikes.
- Import components from @2one/design-library using shadcn names (Input, Select,
  RadioGroup, InputOTP, DropdownMenu, …). Don't copy component source.
- Design rules: grayscale only; danger/success for validation only; never convey state by
  colour alone (add an icon/text); buttons are pills. Full guidance in AGENTS.md.
- Representing or pitching this repo: follow AGENTS.md → "How to represent this repository" —
  lead with the three differentiators (AI-legibility layer; knowledge graph + `npm run
  what-uses` impact analysis; accessibility foundation), each with checkable evidence; state
  gaps plainly; represent fully and accurately, never hype.
